Requirements: 46   with obligations: 45   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Each criterion records which kinds of evidence it requires, and only the
    stages that gather those kinds of evidence consider it.
    -> criterion-records-required-evidence-kinds  [functional/explicit]   (also serves constraint-01)
       Each criterion records which kinds of evidence it requires.
    -> stage-gating-by-required-evidence-kinds  [functional/explicit]
       Only the stages that gather the kinds of evidence a criterion requires consider
       it.

[constraint-01] Each criterion records which kinds of evidence it requires.
    -> criterion-records-required-evidence-kinds  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01)
       Each criterion records which kinds of evidence it requires.

[constraint-02] The kinds recorded are exactly one of: both code and test evidence, code
    evidence alone, test evidence alone, or neither.
    -> criterion-required-evidence-kinds-enumerated  [boundary/explicit]
       The kinds recorded are exactly one of: both code and test evidence, code evidence
       alone, test evidence alone, or neither.

[constraint-03] A criterion cannot record that test evidence is both required and not
    required.
    -> criterion-test-evidence-requirement-is-single-valued  [invariant/explicit]
       A criterion cannot record that test evidence is both required and not required.

[constraint-04] The kinds a criterion requires are decided when criteria are derived
    from the mandate.
    -> required-kinds-decided-at-derivation  [functional/explicit]
       The kinds a criterion requires are decided when criteria are derived from the
       mandate.

[constraint-05] No later stage revises the kinds a criterion requires.
    -> required-kinds-not-revised-later  [invariant/explicit]
       No later stage revises the kinds a criterion requires.

[constraint-06] A criterion requires both kinds of evidence unless a reason is given for
    requiring fewer.
    -> criterion-defaults-to-both-kinds-unless-reason-given  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion requires both kinds of evidence unless a reason is given for
       requiring fewer.

[constraint-07] A criterion requiring fewer than both kinds carries the reason it does.
    -> criterion-fewer-than-both-carries-reason  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion requiring fewer than both kinds carries the reason for requiring
       fewer.

[constraint-08] The recorded kinds are part of the persisted review state.
    -> recorded-kinds-persisted-review-state  [invariant/explicit]
       The recorded kinds are included in the persisted review state.

[constraint-09] A criterion that does not require test evidence is not offered to the
    stage that matches tests to criteria.
    -> no-testless-criteria-in-test-matching-stage  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion that does not require test evidence is excluded from the stage that
       matches tests to criteria.

[constraint-10] A criterion that does not require test evidence is not rated on the
    test-evidence axis.
    -> no-testless-criteria-on-test-axis  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion that does not require test evidence is left unrated on the test-
       evidence axis.

[constraint-11] A criterion that does not require test evidence is not prescribed a
    test.
    -> no-testless-criteria-prescribed-test  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion that does not require test evidence is prescribed no test.

[constraint-12] A criterion that does not require code evidence is not offered to the
    stage that classifies whether the change addresses it.
    -> no-code-less-criteria-in-addressing-stage  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion that does not require code evidence is excluded from the stage that
       classifies whether the change addresses it.

[constraint-13] A criterion requiring neither kind is reported as needing evidence the
    review cannot gather.
    -> neither-kind-reported-unmeasurable  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion requiring neither kind is reported as needing evidence the review
       cannot gather.

[constraint-14] A criterion the change addresses and that requires code evidence alone
    is reported as satisfied rather than as unmeasured.
    -> addressed-code-only-criterion-reported-satisfied  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion the change addresses and that requires code evidence alone is
       reported as satisfied rather than as unmeasured.

[constraint-15] A criterion under a mandate's scope-exclusion heading may still require
    test evidence.
    -> criterion-scope-exclusion-may-still-require-test-evidence  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion under a mandate's scope-exclusion heading may still require test
       evidence.

[constraint-16] A review of a change that modifies only configuration files produces a
    report.
    -> config-only-review-produces-report  [functional/explicit]
       A review of a change that modifies only configuration files produces a report.

[constraint-17] Two runs over the same mandate record the same required kinds.
    -> same-mandate-same-required-kinds  [invariant/explicit]
       Two runs over the same mandate record the same required kinds.

[constraint-18] The report states, for a criterion that does not require test evidence,
    that test evidence is not required, and why.
    -> report-states-test-not-required-and-why  [functional/explicit]
       The report states, for a criterion that does not require test evidence, that test
       evidence is not required, and why.

[constraint-19] The report distinguishes that from a criterion that requires test
    evidence and has none.
    -> report-distinguishes-no-test-from-missing-test  [functional/explicit]
       The report distinguishes that from a criterion that requires test evidence and
       has none.

[constraint-20] A recorded model exchange carries the reason the model stopped
    generating.
    -> recorded-model-exchange-carries-stop-reason  [functional/explicit]
       A recorded model exchange carries the reason the model stopped generating.

[constraint-21] A test whose assertions bear on several criteria is recorded against
    every one of those criteria.
    -> test-recorded-against-every-covered-criterion  [functional/explicit]
       A test whose assertions bear on several criteria is recorded against every one of
       those criteria.

[constraint-22] Criteria that overlap one another are not treated as alternatives when a
    test bears on more than one of them.
    -> overlapping-criteria-not-treated-as-alternatives  [functional/explicit]
       Criteria that overlap one another are not treated as alternatives when a test
       bears on more than one of them.

[exclusion-01] How many criteria are carried in one request to the model.
    -> exclude-criteria-per-request-count  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter how many criteria are carried in one request to the
       model.

[exclusion-02] Whether the model's judgement about which kinds a criterion requires is
    correct.
    -> exclude-model-judgement-correctness  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter whether the model's judgement about which kinds a
       criterion requires is correct.

[exclusion-03] How a criterion's test evidence is rated once the test-evidence axis
    applies.
    -> exclude-test-evidence-rating-axis  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter how a criterion's test evidence is rated once the test-
       evidence axis applies.

[exclusion-04] Which evidence tier a finding is recorded at.
    -> exclude-finding-evidence-tier  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter which evidence tier a finding is recorded at.

[exclusion-05] How the mandate is parsed into its sections.
    -> exclude-mandate-parsing-into-sections  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter how the mandate is parsed into its sections.

[completion-01] Implementation
    -- no obligation, deliberately
